  "contract": [
    "Null configuration, size other than24 or interface mismatch returns10000001 before inspecting the owner. An already nonnull canonical owner returns10000002. Allocate/clear308 bytes and share the existing HRV owner, with no new storage.",
    "Rate groups are the exact finite native lists: odd multiples25 through975, odd multiples50 through950, odd multiples100 through900, and multiples200 through1000. Other32-bit rates use the signed-divide-by25 fallback. Buffer metadata, full-width counts, signed remainder handling and processing defaults match stock.",
    "Storage helper stores supplied pointers/counts without clearing their buffers. Unsupplied buffers allocate wrapping32-bit capacity*4 bytes, return1 on null without changing the record, otherwise clear the requested bytes and write pointer/count/capacity/limit in native order. No16-bit truncation.",
    "The constructor reloads the shared owner around allocator/helper calls, preserves partial failure state without cleanup, allocates48/696-byte auxiliary structures and initializes native metadata. Four signed32 threshold values convert to float32 then divide by exact10000.0f, writing e8/ec/f4/f0.",
    "1273 direct cases execute all982 native instruction bytes. Every integer rate0..1100 is covered, with independent enumerated rate/capacity/storage/processing oracles and exact-Fraction float32 rounding/status calculations for all four FPSCR rounding modes. Only malloc is modeled; actual C storage and memory/string primitives execute.",
    "128 successful full C constructor/actual allocator/complete-teardown lifecycles call no function ports, compare raw complete heap/owner/register/active-FPSCR state, release every allocation to the prior top and clear the canonical HRV owner."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Modeled malloc null returns exercise native guard branches and partial state, not physical exhaustion behavior. The actual public allocator fatal-exhaustion path is nonreturning and separately reconstructed; no claim is made that ordinary allocator exhaustion returns these constructor error codes.",
    "Direct allocator callbacks clone/replace owners to test native reload timing. These are synthetic ordering checks, not proof of safe concurrent ownership replacement. Large wrapping capacities prove header/word arithmetic rather than physically valid buffers.",
    "The fractional oracle covers finite signed-int conversions and division by10000, matching emitted four VCVT.F32.S32 and four VDIV.F32 instructions. Physical FPU delivery/cold activation, invalid pointers, concurrency, caller scratch and private frames remain unproven.",
    "No pointer normalization is needed in the HRV heap replay; raw heap bytes are compared. Five external fatal/logging/system bindings remain available but successful constructor/teardown cases independently assert zero calls.",
    "The892-unit ld-r composition passes without failures or duplicate strong symbols.881 prior nongenerated source/object pairs unchanged, tested object equals normal object, no writable state added. The HRV constructor import is removed without new imports: application76 to75, boot22.",
    "Source-plan/cache layout unchanged. HRV calculation, remaining sensor engines, executor/inference code, final executable linking/startup and hardware boot remain open. This is relocatable composition rather than a bootable firmware image."
  ],
